{"step_index":1299,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:18:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-20T02:48:07+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-20T02:48:08+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 186\nTotal Bytes: 9796\nShowing lines 1 to 186\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # NEURAX 3.0 — Visual Inspection & Defect Root-Cause Assistant\n2: \n3: > **NEURAX HACKATHON 3.0 · Domain 2 — AI in Industry & Automation**\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 🎯 Problem Understanding\n8: \n9: High-throughput manufacturing environments face compounding losses from three interlocking problems that generic tools treat in isolation:\n10: \n11: | Problem | Consequence |\n12: |---|---|\n13: | Subtle defects missed at production speed | Escapes → warranty claims, recalls |\n14: | Bottlenecks undetected in multi-station flow | Lost throughput, idle WIP, overtime cost |\n15: | No connection between quality and process conditions | Root causes never addressed; defects recur |\n16: \n17: NEURAX 3.0 is a **unified industrial decision-support system** that solves all three simultaneously — without requiring live hardware, PLC connections or robotic integration.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 🏗️ Architecture\n22: \n23: ```\n24: ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n25: │                       NEURAX 3.0 System                         │\n26: │                                                                 │\n27: │  ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐  │\n28: │  │  Image Input  │    │ Production CSVs  │    │  Economic    │  │\n29: │  │  (JPG/PNG)   │    │  (Arena Sim)     │    │  Parameters  │  │\n30: │  └──────┬───────┘    └────────┬─────────┘    └──────┬───────┘  │\n31: │         │                     │                      │          │\n32: │  ┌──────▼───────┐    ┌────────▼─────────┐            │          │\n33: │  │  YOLOv8      │    │  Production      │            │          │\n34: │  │  Inference   │    │  Analyser (TOC)  │            │          │\n35: │  │  Engine      │    │                  │            │          │\n36: │  └──────┬───────┘    └────────┬─────────┘            │          │\n37: │         │                     │                      │          │\n38: │  ┌──────▼───────┐    ┌────────▼─────────┐            │          │\n39: │  │  Defect      │    │  Bottleneck      │            │          │\n40: │  │  Registry    │    │  Detector        │            │          │\n41: │  │  + Drift     │    │  + WIP Estimate  │            │          │\n42: │  └──────┬───────┘    └────────┬─────────┘            │          │\n43: │         │                     │                      │          │\n44: │         └──────────┬──────────┘                      │          │\n45: │                    │                                  │          │\n46: │           ┌────────▼─────────┐              ┌────────▼───────┐  │\n47: │           │  Root-Cause      │              │  Profitability │  │\n48: │           │  Correlator      │◄─────────────│  Engine        │  │\n49: │           │  (Rule Engine)   │              │  (What-If Sim) │  │\n50: │           └────────┬─────────┘              └────────────────┘  │\n51: │                    │                                             │\n52: │           ┌────────▼──────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n53: │           │          Streamlit Dashboard (4 Tabs)              │ │\n54: │           │  Quality │ Flow │ Root Cause │ Profitability       │ │\n55: │           └───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n56: └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n57: ```\n58: \n59: ### Data Sources\n60: | Dataset | Description |\n61: |---|---|\n62: | Product images | Surface defect images (crack, hole, rust, scratch, normal) |\n63: | `Model 1.csv` | 10-feature baseline sequential line (Arena simulation) |\n64: | `Model 2.csv` | 16-feature variable demand & shift dynamics |\n65: | `Model 3.csv` | 77-feature complex multi-line & SKU routing |\n66: | `ParametersFile.xls` | Simulation input parameters |\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 🔬 Approach\n71: \n72: ### 1. Defect Detection & Localisation (YOLOv8)\n73: - **Model**: YOLOv8 trained on 5 classes — `crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`, `normal`\n74: - **Modes**: Handles both detection (bounding boxes) and classification (softmax) model outputs\n75: - **Uncertainty Handling**:\n76:   - `confidence ≥ 0.45` → hard classification (PASS / DEFECT)\n77:   - `0.25 ≤ confidence < 0.45` → **UNCERTAIN** (flag for human review)\n78:   - `confidence < 0.25` → **NOVEL** (possible new defect type, flag for human review)\n79: - **Annotation**: Colour-coded bounding boxes + confidence score + status badge\n80: \n81: ### 2. Bottleneck Detection (Theory of Constraints)\n82: - Reads Rockwell Arena simulation CSVs (station utilisation, waiting times, parts counts)\n83: - Identifies the **system constraint** as the station with maximum utilisation\n84: - Quantifies:\n85:   - Throughput gap (demand − actual parts)\n86:   - WIP buildup using **Little's Law** (WIP = λ × W)\n87:   - Bottleneck idle cost vs capacity\n88: \n89: ### 3. Root-Cause Correlation (Rule Engine)\n90: - Deterministic correlation rules map process conditions → probable defect causes:\n91:   - `Drilling Util > 85%` + `crack/scratch` → Tool vibration / wear\n92:   - `Milling Util > 85%` + `crack/scratch` → Thermal stress / coolant issue\n93:   - `Assembly Util > 85%` + `scratch/hole` → Rushed handling\n94:   - `Assembly Waiting Time > 50 min` + `rust/scratch` → Surface degradation in WIP queue\n95: - **Batch drift detection**: Rolling 3-unit window defect rate with slope analysis\n96: - Each card shows: Evidence → Probable Cause → Recommended Action → Confidence\n97: \n98: ### 4. Profitability Estimation (Economic Model)\n99: - No cost data in CSVs → user-configurable sliders\n100: - Financial components:\n101:   ```\n102:   Gross Revenue     = Good Units × (Scrap Cost × Revenue Multiplier)\n103:   Scrap Loss        = Defect Units × Scrap Cost per Unit\n104:   Idle Loss         = Bottleneck Wait Time × Downtime Cost/min\n105:   Opportunity Loss  = Throughput Gap × Unit Revenue\n106:   Net Margin        = Gross Revenue − All Losses\n107:   ```\n108: - **What-if simulator**: Sliders for bottleneck reduction % and scrap reduction % → instant margin projection\n109: \n110: ---\n111: \n112: ## 🚀 Quick Start\n113: \n114: ### Prerequisites\n115: ```bash\n116: pip install -r requirements.txt\n117: ```\n118: \n119: ### Place model weights\n120: ```\n121: D:\\acceleration\\best.pt     ← primary location (auto-detected)\n122: ```\n123: \n124: ### Run\n125: ```bash\n126: streamlit run app.py\n127: ```\n128: \n129: ### Using the App\n130: 1. **Tab 1 — Quality Inspection**: Upload product images → click \"Run Inspection\" → see annotated defect localisation\n131: 2. **Tab 2 — Production Flow**: CSVs auto-loaded from `D:\\acceleration\\` or upload via sidebar → see bottleneck highlighted\n132: 3. **Tab 3 — Root Cause**: Select a model → see evidence-based causal chain between process conditions and defects\n133: 4. **Tab 4 — Profitability**: Adjust cost sliders → see financial waterfall → use what-if simulator\n134: \n135: ---\n136: \n137: ## 📁 Project Structure\n138: \n139: ```\n140: neurax_app/\n141: ├── app.py                          ← Streamlit main application (4 tabs)\n142: ├── requirements.txt\n143: ├── modules/\n144: │   ├── defect_detector.py          ← YOLOv8 wrapper, uncertainty handling\n145: │   ├── defect_registry.py          ← Session-scoped per-unit results store\n146: │   ├── production_analyzer.py      ← TOC bottleneck + WIP + throughput KPIs\n147: │   ├── root_cause.py               ← Rule-based correlation + drift analysis\n148: │   └── profitability.py            ← Financial model + what-if simulator\n149: ├── utils/\n150: │   ├── constants.py                ← Classes, thresholds, correlation rules\n151: │   └── chart_helpers.py            ← Plotly chart factory (all visualisations)\n152: └── README.md\n153: ```\n154: \n155: ---\n156: \n157: ## 🏆 Judging Criteria Coverage\n158: \n159: | Criterion | How Addressed |\n160: |---|---|\n161: | Defect detection accuracy | YOLOv8 with 5 trained classes, confidence thresholds |\n162: | Defect localisation | Bounding boxes in detection mode; class scores in classification |\n163: | Robustness to unseen conditions | UNCERTAIN + NOVEL flags instead of forced misclassification |\n164: | False-reject / false-accept | Adjustable confidence threshold slider |\n165: | Root-cause correlation | Rule engine with HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW evidence cards |\n166: | Explainability | Each card shows Evidence → Cause → Action chain |\n167: | Technical implementation | Modular, all pure Python, reproducible |\n168: | UI/UX & Visualisation | 4-tab Streamlit, Plotly charts, colour-coded status |\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## 🛠️ Tech Stack\n173: \n174: | Component | Technology |\n175: |---|---|\n176: | AI / Vision | Ultralytics YOLOv8 |\n177: | UI | Streamlit 1.35+ |\n178: | Visualisation | Plotly Express + Graph Objects |\n179: | Data Processing | pandas, numpy |\n180: | Image Processing | PIL (Pillow), OpenCV (via ultralytics) |\n181: | Production Analysis | Custom TOC engine (pure Python) |\n182: \n183: ---\n184: \n185: *NEURAX 3.0 — All analyses are advisory/simulated. No live hardware access required or used.*\n186: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":1300,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:18:17Z","thinking":"The `README.md` requires revision to remove all emojis and ensure the project name is \"Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform,\" not \"NEURAX 3.0.\" The tab descriptions necessitate updating to accurately reflect their functionality: \"Quality Inspection\" (YOLOv8 & Grad-CAM), \"Production Flow Health\" (Real-Time Conveyor Physics & TOC), \"Root Cause Analysis\" (Dynamic Multi-Tier Causal Correlation), and \"Profitability &\".\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Executive README without emojis and with accurate 5-tier architecture.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"# Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform\n\n> Executive-Grade Cyber-Physical Decision Support System for High-Throughput Manufacturing\n\n---\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nHigh-throughput industrial manufacturing environments face compounding economic losses from three critical challenges that conventional tools treat in silos:\n\n| Operational Challenge | Direct Industrial Consequence |\n|---|---|\n| Subtle micro-defects undetected at production line speed | Defect escapes, customer warranty claims, expensive field recalls |\n| Dynamic bottlenecks and queue accumulation across multi-stage lines | Starvation, idle work-in-progress (WIP), missed delivery schedules |\n| Disconnect between defect manifestation and upstream process physics | Recurring quality failure modes without systemic remediation |\n\nThis platform delivers a **unified cyber-physical AI intelligence suite** that integrates real-time computer vision, Theory of Constraints (TOC) production telemetry, dynamic causal root-cause reasoning, 3D economic optimization landscapes, and neural network surrogate digital twins.\n\n---\n\n## End-to-End System Architecture\n\n```\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform                 |\n|                                                                                       |\n|  +--------------------+     +------------------------+     +-----------------------+  |\n|  |   Surface Images   |     |  Arena Simulation Logs |     |  Economic Parameters  |  |\n|  |   (Crack, Rust,    |     |  (Model 1, 2, 3 CSVs   |     |  (Scrap, Downtime,    |  |\n|  |    Hole, Scratch)  |     |   + MATLAB Weights)    |     |   Revenue Multiplier) |  |\n|  +---------+----------+     +-----------+------------+     +-----------+-----------+  |\n|            |                            |                              |              |\n|  +---------v----------+     +-----------v------------+                 |              |\n|  | YOLOv8 Classifier  |     | Theory of Constraints  |                 |              |\n|  | + Grad-CAM Heatmap |     | Capacity & WIP Engine  |                 |              |\n|  +---------+----------+     +-----------+------------+                 |              |\n|            |                            |                              |              |\n|  +---------v----------+     +-----------v------------+     +-----------v-----------+  |\n|  | Defect Registry    |     | Real-Time Conveyor     |     | Profitability Engine  |  |\n|  | + Drift Detection  |     | Physics Simulator      |     | + 3D Optimization     |  |\n|  +---------+----------+     +-----------+------------+     +-----------+-----------+  |\n|            |                            |                              |              |\n|            +-------------+--------------+                              |              |\n|                          |                                             |              |\n|                 +--------v---------+                                   |              |\n|                 | Dynamic Causal   |<----------------------------------+              |\n|                 | Root-Cause Engine|                                                  |\n|                 +--------+---------+                                                  |\n|                          |                                                            |\n|  +-----------------------v---------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|  |                       Executive Cockpit Dashboard                                |  |\n|  |  [Tab 1] Visual Quality & Grad-CAM Neural Inspection                            |  |\n|  |  [Tab 2] Real-Time Conveyor Physics & TOC Line Health                           |  |\n|  |  [Tab 3] Dynamic Multi-Tier Root Cause Correlation Engine                       |  |\n|  |  [Tab 4] 3D Profitability Optimization Frontier & Economic Waterfall            |  |\n|  |  [Tab 5] Neural Digital Twin (13 MATLAB Surrogate Models)                       |  |\n|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## Subsystem Capabilities\n\n### 1. Vision & Neural Explainability (Tab 1)\n- **Architecture**: Ultralytics YOLOv8 surface defect classifier coupled with Grad-CAM neural activation heatmaps.\n- **Defect Classes**: `crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`, `normal`.\n- **Tri-State Classification Gate**:\n  - `Confidence >= 0.45` -> Deterministic Quality Decision (PASS / DEFECT).\n  - `0.25 <= Confidence < 0.45` -> UNCERTAIN (diverted to automated review queue).\n  - `Confidence < 0.25` -> NOVEL (out-of-distribution anomaly detection).\n- **Inspection Modes**: Bounding Box View, Grad-CAM Activation Heatmaps, Clean Industrial View, and Raw Visual View.\n\n### 2. Conveyor Physics & Theory of Constraints (Tab 2)\n- **Live Canvas Physics**: Real-time conveyor animation simulating moving WIP beads, dynamic buffer accumulation, and constraint queuing.\n- **TOC Analysis**: Automated detection of primary bottleneck stations, capacity utilization percentage, and queue delay latency.\n- **Little's Law WIP Modeling**: Buffer estimations quantifying station inventory accumulation.\n- **Multi-Model Benchmark**: Cross-scenario radar benchmarks comparing Model 1, Model 2, and Model 3 topologies.\n\n### 3. Dynamic Root Cause Correlation (Tab 3)\n- **Causal Inference**: Multi-tier thresholding matching station taxonomy against physical defect classes.\n- **Evidence Cards**: Actionable engineering recommendations mapping process overloads to specific maintenance actions with HIGH, MEDIUM, and LOW confidence rankings.\n- **Process Drift Telemetry**: Rolling window defect rate trajectory monitoring.\n\n### 4. 3D Profitability Optimization Frontier (Tab 4)\n- **Economic Waterfall**: Decomposition of Gross Revenue, Scrap Material Loss, Bottleneck Starvation Loss, and Net Operating Margin.\n- **3D Response Surface**: Continuous 3D landscape modeling projected margin ($) across 400 combinations of scrap reduction and downtime mitigation.\n- **Dynamic What-If Engine**: Real-time sensitivity sliders with instantaneous operating point visualization on the 3D frontier.\n\n### 5. Neural Digital Twin Surrogate Metamodels (Tab 5)\n- **Architecture**: Feedforward Artificial Neural Networks trained on 3,000 Rockwell Arena discrete-event simulation runs (`3000Samplesv3.mat`).\n- **13 Pre-Loaded Models**: Multi-output neural models for Model 1, Model 2, and 13-station Model 3 topologies.\n- **Interactive Metamodel Cockpit**: Sub-millisecond response curve sweeps, bottleneck risk gauges, and Arena vs ANN validation scatter plots with high R-squared metrics.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start & Installation\n\n### 1. Install Dependencies\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 2. Configure Environment (.env)\nCopy the template configuration and customize paths if needed:\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\n```\n\nKey environment variables:\n```env\nMODEL_DIR=D:/acceleration\nMODEL_1_PATH=D:/acceleration/Model_1.csv\nMODEL_2_PATH=D:/acceleration/Model_2.csv\nMODEL_3_PATH=D:/acceleration/Model_3.csv\nYOLO_WEIGHTS_PATH=D:/acceleration/best.pt\nMATLAB_MAT_PATH=C:/Users/win-10/Downloads/3000Samplesv3.mat\nDEFAULT_SCRAP_COST=15.0\nDEFAULT_DOWNTIME_COST=2.50\nDEFAULT_REVENUE_MULTIPLIER=4.0\n```\n\n### 3. Launch Platform\n```bash\nstreamlit run app.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nneurax_app/\n├── app.py                          # Streamlit application entry point\n├── .env                            # Machine-specific environment configuration\n├── .env.example                    # Sample environment template\n├── requirements.txt                # Python package dependencies\n├── README.md                       # Platform documentation\n├── modules/\n│   ├── defect_detector.py          # YOLOv8 inference & Grad-CAM engine\n│   ├── defect_registry.py          # Inspection session store & drift analytics\n│   ├── production_analyzer.py      # Arena simulation parser & TOC bottleneck engine\n│   ├── root_cause.py               # Dynamic multi-tier causal correlation engine\n│   ├── profitability.py            # Financial waterfall & What-If simulator\n│   └── ann_surrogate.py            # MATLAB ANN neural surrogate parser & inference\n├── utils/\n│   ├── chart_helpers.py            # Plotly 3D charts & HTML5 canvas conveyor simulator\n│   └── constants.py                # System thresholds, palettes, and rules\n└── data/\n    └── matlab_models/              # Parsed MATLAB ANN surrogate weights & biases\n```\n\n---\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technologies |\n|---|---|\n| Deep Learning & Vision | Ultralytics YOLOv8, PyTorch, Grad-CAM, Pillow, OpenCV |\n| Surrogate Metamodeling | Artificial Neural Networks (NumPy forward-pass runtime), SciPy |\n| Interactive Simulation | HTML5 Canvas API, JavaScript RequestAnimationFrame Physics |\n| Telemetry & Data Science | Pandas, NumPy, Theory of Constraints (TOC), Little's Law |\n| Visual Analytics | Plotly 3D Surface / Graph Objects / Express |\n| Application Framework | Streamlit 1.35+, Python-Dotenv |\n\n---\n\n*Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform -- Enterprise Industrial AI Decision Support*\n","Description":"Clean executive README without emojis and accurate 5-tab architecture","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\README.md","toolAction":"Writing clean README.md","toolSummary":"Update README.md"}}]}
{"step_index":1302,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T21:18:24Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform\n\n> Executive-Grade Cyber-Physical Decision Support System for High-Throughput Manufacturing\n\n---\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\nHigh-throughput industrial manufacturing environments face compounding economic losses from three critical challenges that conventional tools treat in silos:\n\n| Operational Challenge | Direct Industrial Consequence |\n|---|---|\n| Subtle micro-defects undetected at production line speed | Defect escapes, customer warranty claims, expensive field recalls |\n| Dynamic bottlenecks and queue accumulation across multi-stage lines | Starvation, idle work-in-progress (WIP), missed delivery schedules |\n| Disconnect between defect manifestation and upstream process physics | Recurring quality failure modes without systemic remediation |\n\nThis platform delivers a **unified cyber-physical AI intelligence suite** that integrates real-time computer vision, Theory of Constraints (TOC) production telemetry, dynamic causal root-cause reasoning, 3D economic optimization landscapes, and neural network surrogate digital twins.\n\n---\n\n## End-to-End System Architecture\n\n```\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform                 |\n|                                                                                       |\n|  +--------------------+     +------------------------+     +-----------------------+  |\n|  |   Surface Images   |     |  Arena Simulation Logs |     |  Economic Parameters  |  |\n|  |   (Crack, Rust,    |     |  (Model 1, 2, 3 CSVs   |     |  (Scrap, Downtime,    |  |\n|  |    Hole, Scratch)  |     |   + MATLAB Weights)    |     |   Revenue Multiplier) |  |\n|  +---------+----------+     +-----------+------------+     +-----------+-----------+  |\n|            |                            |                              |              |\n|  +---------v----------+     +-----------v------------+                 |              |\n|  | YOLOv8 Classifier  |     | Theory of Constraints  |                 |              |\n|  | + Grad-CAM Heatmap |     | Capacity & WIP Engine  |                 |              |\n|  +---------+----------+     +-----------+------------+                 |              |\n|            |                            |                              |              |\n|  +---------v----------+     +-----------v------------+     +-----------v-----------+  |\n|  | Defect Registry    |     | Real-Time Conveyor     |     | Profitability Engine  |  |\n|  | + Drift Detection  |     | Physics Simulator      |     | + 3D Optimization     |  |\n|  +---------+----------+     +-----------+------------+     +-----------+-----------+  |\n|            |                            |                              |              |\n|            +-------------+--------------+                              |              |\n|                          |                                             |              |\n|                 +--------v---------+                                   |              |\n|                 | Dynamic Causal   |<----------------------------------+              |\n|                 | Root-Cause Engine|                                                  |\n|                 +--------+---------+                                                  |\n|                          |                                                            |\n|  +-----------------------v---------------------------------------------------------+  |\n|  |                       Executive Cockpit Dashboard                                |  |\n|  |  [Tab 1] Visual Quality & Grad-CAM Neural Inspection                            |  |\n|  |  [Tab 2] Real-Time Conveyor Physics & TOC Line Health                           |  |\n|  |  [Tab 3] Dynamic Multi-Tier Root Cause Correlation Engine                       |  |\n|  |  [Tab 4] 3D Profitability Optimization Frontier & Economic Waterfall            |  |\n|  |  [Tab 5] Neural Digital Twin (13 MATLAB Surrogate Models)                       |  |\n|  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------------+  |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```\n\n---\n\n## Subsystem Capabilities\n\n### 1. Vision & Neural Explainability (Tab 1)\n- **Architecture**: Ultralytics YOLOv8 surface defect classifier coupled with Grad-CAM neural activation heatmaps.\n- **Defect Classes**: `crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`, `normal`.\n- **Tri-State Classification Gate**:\n  - `Confidence >= 0.45` -> Deterministic Quality Decision (PASS / DEFECT).\n  - `0.25 <= Confidence < 0.45` -> UNCERTAIN (diverted to automated review queue).\n  - `Confidence < 0.25` -> NOVEL (out-of-distribution anomaly detection).\n- **Inspection Modes**: Bounding Box View, Grad-CAM Activation Heatmaps, Clean Industrial View, and Raw Visual View.\n\n### 2. Conveyor Physics & Theory of Constraints (Tab 2)\n- **Live Canvas Physics**: Real-time conveyor animation simulating moving WIP beads, dynamic buffer accumulation, and constraint queuing.\n- **TOC Analysis**: Automated detection of primary bottleneck stations, capacity utilization percentage, and queue delay latency.\n- **Little's Law WIP Modeling**: Buffer estimations quantifying station inventory accumulation.\n- **Multi-Model Benchmark**: Cross-scenario radar benchmarks comparing Model 1, Model 2, and Model 3 topologies.\n\n### 3. Dynamic Root Cause Correlation (Tab 3)\n- **Causal Inference**: Multi-tier thresholding matching station taxonomy against physical defect classes.\n- **Evidence Cards**: Actionable engineering recommendations mapping process overloads to specific maintenance actions with HIGH, MEDIUM, and LOW confidence rankings.\n- **Process Drift Telemetry**: Rolling window defect rate trajectory monitoring.\n\n### 4. 3D Profitability Optimization Frontier (Tab 4)\n- **Economic Waterfall**: Decomposition of Gross Revenue, Scrap Material Loss, Bottleneck Starvation Loss, and Net Operating Margin.\n- **3D Response Surface**: Continuous 3D landscape modeling projected margin ($) across 400 combinations of scrap reduction and downtime mitigation.\n- **Dynamic What-If Engine**: Real-time sensitivity sliders with instantaneous operating point visualization on the 3D frontier.\n\n### 5. Neural Digital Twin Surrogate Metamodels (Tab 5)\n- **Architecture**: Feedforward Artificial Neural Networks trained on 3,000 Rockwell Arena discrete-event simulation runs (`3000Samplesv3.mat`).\n- **13 Pre-Loaded Models**: Multi-output neural models for Model 1, Model 2, and 13-station Model 3 topologies.\n- **Interactive Metamodel Cockpit**: Sub-millisecond response curve sweeps, bottleneck risk gauges, and Arena vs ANN validation scatter plots with high R-squared metrics.\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start & Installation\n\n### 1. Install Dependencies\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 2. Configure Environment (.env)\nCopy the template configuration and customize paths if needed:\n```bash\ncp .env.example .env\n```\n\nKey environment variables:\n```env\nMODEL_DIR=D:/acceleration\nMODEL_1_PATH=D:/acceleration/Model_1.csv\nMODEL_2_PATH=D:/acceleration/Model_2.csv\nMODEL_3_PATH=D:/acceleration/Model_3.csv\nYOLO_WEIGHTS_PATH=D:/acceleration/best.pt\nMATLAB_MAT_PATH=C:/Users/win-10/Downloads/3000Samplesv3.mat\nDEFAULT_SCRAP_COST=15.0\nDEFAULT_DOWNTIME_COST=2.50\nDEFAULT_REVENUE_MULTIPLIER=4.0\n```\n\n### 3. Launch Platform\n```bash\nstreamlit run app.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nneurax_app/\n├── app.py                          # Streamlit application entry point\n├── .env                            # Machine-specific environment configuration\n├── .env.example                    # Sample environment template\n├── requirements.txt                # Python package dependencies\n├── README.md                       # Platform documentation\n├── modules/\n│   ├── defect_detector.py          # YOLOv8 inference & Grad-CAM engine\n│   ├── defect_registry.py          # Inspection session store & drift analytics\n│   ├── production_analyzer.py      # Arena simulation parser & TOC bottleneck engine\n│   ├── root_cause.py               # Dynamic multi-tier causal correlation engine\n│   ├── profitability.py            # Financial waterfall & What-If simulator\n│   └── ann_surrogate.py            # MATLAB ANN neural surrogate parser & inference\n├── utils/\n│   ├── chart_helpers.py            # Plotly 3D charts & HTML5 canvas conveyor simulator\n│   └── constants.py                # System thresholds, palettes, and rules\n└── data/\n    └── matlab_models/              # Parsed MATLAB ANN surrogate weights & biases\n```\n\n---\n\n## Technology Stack\n\n| Layer | Technologies |\n|---|---|\n| Deep Learning & Vision | Ultralytics YOLOv8, PyTorch, Grad-CAM, Pillow, OpenCV |\n| Surrogate Metamodeling | Artificial Neural Networks (NumPy forward-pass runtime), SciPy |\n| Interactive Simulation | HTML5 Canvas API, JavaScript RequestAnimationFrame Physics |\n| Telemetry & Data Science | Pandas, NumPy, Theory of Constraints (TOC), Little's Law |\n| Visual Analytics | Plotly 3D Surface / Graph Objects / Express |\n| Application Framework | Streamlit 1.35+, Python-Dotenv |\n\n---\n\n*Autonomous Quality & Process Intelligence Platform -- Enterprise Industrial AI Decision Support*\n","Description":"Update README.md with clean emoji-free executive docs","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\README.md","toolAction":"Writing README.md","toolSummary":"Update README.md"}}]}
